# Explicitly recursive (not just "node_modules"): a bare, unanchored pattern
# does NOT reliably exclude nested directories like backend/node_modules or
# packages/*/node_modules in every builder (confirmed empirically — Podman's
# builder here only matched it at the context root). This matters now that
# backend/ is included in this context too (see the note below) — without
# this, COPY backend/ . in backend/Dockerfile would pull in the *host's own*
# backend/node_modules, silently overwriting the correct node_modules that
# Dockerfile's own npm ci step had just built inside the image, with a stale,
# host-absolute-path @money/domain symlink pointing nowhere in the container.
**/node_modules
dist
.angular
.vscode
*.log
.env
.git
.gitignore
*.md
.DS_Store
coverage
.firebase
*.spec.ts
e2e
.editorconfig
karma.conf.js
.browserslistrc
# NOT ignored: backend/ — backend/Dockerfile now also builds from this same
# root context (see its header comment) and needs backend/ visible to its own
# COPY steps. Harmless for the frontend image: its COPY . . only feeds an
# intermediate build stage discarded before the final nginx stage, so this
# adds build-time I/O only, never final image size or content.
k8s
docs
*.sh
*.ps1
# apps/mcp/Dockerfile needs docs/api/openapi.yaml (schema generation) and
# docs/domain/ (explain_concept's content, loaded at runtime — see that
# Dockerfile's header comment) despite the blanket `docs`/`*.md` excludes
# above. Un-ignoring a nested path requires un-ignoring each ancestor
# directory too, not just the file pattern — an ignored directory is never
# traversed, so a deeper negation alone has nothing to override. Harmless
# for the other Dockerfiles for the same reason as the backend/ note above.
!docs
!docs/api
!docs/api/openapi.yaml
!docs/domain
!docs/domain/*.md
